WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.585
Welcome to the Concilium Security Risk Brief for Monday, November twenty third.

2
00:00:04.585 --> 00:00:11.993
Five minutes of security coverage from the last twenty four hours, to increase your situational awareness without decreasing your productivity.

3
00:00:11.993 --> 00:00:14.429
Here's what matters today.

4
00:00:14.429 --> 00:00:28.934
Today: Ukraine says it sank a Russian warship in a Libyan port, troops in northern Nigeria rescue most of a group of abducted children, a deadly Russian strike near Kyiv, Houthi attacks on Saudi infrastructure, and an update on Ebola in Congo.

5
00:00:28.934 --> 00:00:30.269
We start in Libya.

6
00:00:30.269 --> 00:00:38.661
Reuters reports President Volodymyr Zelenskiy said Ukraine sank the Russian naval corvette Merkury in a Libyan port using seven naval drones.

7
00:00:38.661 --> 00:00:47.399
Radio Free Europe Radio Liberty reports Libya says a suspected sea drone caused an explosion aboard a Russian ship docked at a naval base near Benghazi, injuring ten Russian and Libyan crew members.

8
00:00:47.399 --> 00:00:55.762
The Institute for the Study of War says Ukrainian forces struck two Russian vessels near Benghazi, destroying at least one.

9
00:00:55.762 --> 00:00:57.352
Next, Nigeria.

10
00:00:57.352 --> 00:01:11.429
Voice of Nigeria reports the Nigerian Army says troops rescued eighteen of twenty two children from the Boys' and Girls' Brigade who were abducted by suspected terrorists during an early morning road walk in the Mother Cat community, in the Kachia and Kajuru area of Kaduna State.

11
00:01:11.429 --> 00:01:14.626
The army says the search for the other four continues.

12
00:01:14.626 --> 00:01:17.579
The terrorism monitor TRAC also reported the rescue.

13
00:01:17.579 --> 00:01:20.896
Turning to Ukraine.

14
00:01:20.896 --> 00:01:27.324
Reuters reports a Russian attack on Dymer, in the Kyiv region, killed eleven people, according to an official.

15
00:01:27.324 --> 00:01:36.155
Earlier, Reuters reported President Zelenskiy said at least fourteen people were missing after a Russian drone hit a building in the region.

16
00:01:36.155 --> 00:01:47.131
In Saudi Arabia, the Institute for the Study of War and Critical Threats say the Houthi movement targeted Saudi critical infrastructure on Saturday and Sunday, November twenty first and twenty second, and claimed a strike on Petro Rabigh oil facilities.

17
00:01:47.131 --> 00:01:55.732
They describe it as part of a campaign to press Saudi Arabia to end military operations in Yemen.

18
00:01:55.732 --> 00:01:58.551
And an update on the Ebola outbreak in Congo.

19
00:01:58.551 --> 00:02:04.961
Reuters reports the head of the World Health Organization says fighting near the outbreak area is disrupting the response.

20
00:02:04.961 --> 00:02:14.703
A separate Reuters analysis of satellite imagery shows graveyards in eastern Congo expanding much faster than the official Ebola death count, pointing to a major undercount.

21
00:02:14.703 --> 00:02:16.821
Now a few quick notes by region.

22
00:02:16.821 --> 00:02:24.813
In Europe, an update on Friday, November twentieth: Reuters reports Polish prosecutors say three Russian missiles flew into Poland that day.

23
00:02:24.813 --> 00:02:32.497
The Institute for the Study of War says a Russian jet powered drone violated Moldovan airspace twice on Saturday, November twenty first.

24
00:02:32.497 --> 00:02:41.781
And in England, Reuters reports thousands of people were evacuated from a concert in Manchester last night after reports that an unknown substance had been released, British police said.

25
00:02:41.781 --> 00:02:52.832
In Africa, the International Committee of the Red Cross says intensifying hostilities in Ethiopia's Tigray region have forced health facilities to suspend services.

26
00:02:52.832 --> 00:02:53.981
In the Pacific, the U.S.

27
00:02:53.981 --> 00:03:00.556
Geological Survey reported a preliminary magnitude six point five earthquake in the Vanuatu region.

28
00:03:00.556 --> 00:03:01.942
That's today's brief.

29
00:03:01.942 --> 00:03:10.053
These security developments come from government travel advisories and trusted analysts, curated by the Concilium Security Risk Management Team.

30
00:03:10.053 --> 00:03:18.277
The brief summarizes public reporting and isn't a substitute for your own risk assessment, so check the original source before making travel decisions.

31
00:03:18.277 --> 00:03:20.375
This brief is digitally narrated.

32
00:03:20.375 --> 00:03:21.295
Questions?

33
00:03:21.295 --> 00:03:24.742
Reach Concilium at info at concilium dot U.S.

34
00:03:24.742 --> 00:03:26.657
Thanks for listening, and stay safe.
